## Quality Gates (Go / No-Go)

### Architecture (Clean Architecture)

- [ ] `domain` has no import from `data`, `presentation`, React or React Native
- [ ] Repository has an interface in `domain` and implementation in `data`
- [ ] Each UseCase resolves a single business action
- [ ] View only talks to its ViewModel (no direct Repository/DataSource access)
- [ ] Code placed in the correct layer and scope (feature vs shared)

### Conventions

- [ ] Path aliases used consistently
- [ ] No hardcoded endpoint URL (centralized in `core`/constants)
- [ ] Avoid `any` when domain typing is possible
- [ ] Naming follows `code-conventions.mdc` (Entity/UseCase/Repository/DataSource suffixes)

### Tests

- [ ] UseCase logic validated in domain tests (no RN mocks needed)
- [ ] Repository implementation validated with DataSource mocked
- [ ] ViewModel validated with UseCase mocked
- [ ] View behavior validated with ViewModel mocked

No-Go if any mandatory item above is unresolved.

---

## Quick Anti-Patterns

- Business logic inside the View layer
- Domain importing from data/presentation (breaks dependency rule)
- Creating a shared component for one-feature-only usage
- Calling a DataSource/Repository directly from a ViewModel bypassing the UseCase
- Hardcoded endpoints/colors/fonts in new code
- Testing business logic only via UI tests (without UseCase/domain tests)

